<main id="inicio">
<section class="portada">
<div class="envoltura"><div class="pagina">
<div class="eti">Safety</div>
<h1>Is ManaLab safe? How to check it yourself</h1>
<p class="lead">ManaLab is a free tool made by one person. It isn't code-signed yet and the code isn't public, so being careful is reasonable. This page says exactly what it does and how to check it, so you don't have to take my word for it.</p>
</div></div>
</section>
<div class="cuerpo">
<div class="envoltura"><div class="pagina">
<section class="tarjeta" id="lee">
<h2>What it reads and what it touches</h2>
<ul><li>It reads <code>Player.log</code> and the card database Arena leaves on your PC, without changing them. <code>Player.log</code> is the file Arena writes when “Detailed Logs (Plugin Support)” is turned on in its settings.</li><li>For Magic Online it reads <code>mtgo.log</code>, the <code>Match_GameLog_*.dat</code> files, <code>mtgo_game_history</code> and the <code>grouping *.xml</code> files it leaves on your PC, also without changing them.</li><li>It doesn't modify Arena or Magic Online, doesn't read their memory and doesn't connect to Wizards' servers.</li><li>It takes no screenshots on its own. It saves an image of the game window on your PC only when you ask for a highlighted moment (F8, the button over the game or “Capture moment”).</li><li>Your games, screenshots and stats stay in a folder on your PC, except what you share yourself: team mode, exporting a game or the AI analysis.</li></ul>
</section>
<section class="tarjeta" id="conexiones">
<h2>Every connection it makes</h2>
<ol><li>Once a day it asks GitHub (<code>api.github.com</code>) if there's a new version (if GitHub doesn't answer, it checks <code>manalab.es/version.json</code>). Only if you press “Update now” does it download the new ZIP and its SHA-256 from <code>github.com</code>.</li><li>Every 3 days it downloads the updated meta deck lists, one per format, from a public repository (<code>raw.githubusercontent.com</code>): <a href="https://github.com/EusebioG96/registro-mtga-meta" rel="noopener">github.com/EusebioG96/registro-mtga-meta</a></li><li>It queries Scryfall (<code>api.scryfall.com</code>) with card ids (Arena and Magic Online) or names for missing names, the overlay and the replay images, and downloads the card images from <code>cards.scryfall.io</code>.</li><li>When it opens and every 6 hours it downloads a small content file from manalab.es (<code>manalab.es/contenido.json</code>, such as the support link, which features to show or the creators shown in Learn). It sends nothing of yours except the ManaLab version.</li><li>At the end of the Dashboard it loads <code>manalab.es/anuncio/</code>, which shows an ad from the Metafy network: that page loads the ad script from <code>mdn.metafy.gg</code>. Metafy receives at least the ad request, like any website (IP, browser); ManaLab passes it no data from your games.</li><li>The Learn section asks a ManaLab server for its list of guides when you open it (at most once an hour), sending only the ManaLab version. The guide covers load from Metafy (<code>metafy.gg</code>) and the creators' photos from <code>manalab.es</code>, with no referrer. Those servers see the request like any website (IP, browser).</li><li>The app and the Learn page send a ManaLab server (<code>workers.dev</code>), at most once an hour, the figures of the featured creators: how many times each was seen and clicked, as totals only.</li></ol>
<p>You can turn the first three off in Settings. The ad is removed with the X or in Settings › Data and about ManaLab. The content file and the Learn section have no switch of their own. They send nothing from your games, your PC or your account: the content file sends only the ManaLab version, and the Learn section sends the ManaLab version (in the app) and the featured creators' figures, as totals only. The links you click open in your browser, outside ManaLab.</p>
<p>On this website, pages with an ad load the Metafy network script (<code>mdn.metafy.gg</code>): Metafy receives the visit like any website (IP, browser and the page). The Learn page asks a ManaLab server (<code>workers.dev</code>) for the list of guides and Metafy (<code>metafy.gg</code>) for the covers, with no cookies or referrer. The user guides, this page, the privacy policy and the error page do not show ads.</p>
<p>Only if you use them: AI analysis, bug reports (both go to a ManaLab server on Cloudflare Workers, <code>workers.dev</code>) and team mode (a shared folder you choose).</p>
<p>When you press the AI analysis button on a lost game, it sends that game's data (result, deck, hands, cards seen and timeline), with no player names (the name you give your deck is included).</p>
<p>When you send a bug report from Settings, our server receives what you write, your email if you add one, the app version, your system and language, whether Arena and Magic Online are in use, an anonymous ID of your PC and, if you tick it, the last lines of <code>registro.log</code> without your username or codes. No games or decks are sent. The server forwards it by email and does not store it. More in the <a href="/privacy/#en">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</section>
<section class="tarjeta" id="comprobar">
<h2>How to check the file you downloaded</h2>
<ol><li>Every release has its <a href="https://github.com/EusebioG96/ManaLab/releases/latest" rel="noopener">SHA-256</a> and a <a href="https://github.com/EusebioG96/ManaLab/releases/latest" rel="noopener">VirusTotal scan</a>.</li><li>In PowerShell, from the folder with the ZIP:<div class="cmd"><code>Get-FileHash .\ManaLab*.zip -Algorithm SHA256</code></div>The result should match the one I publish.</li><li>If you prefer, upload the ZIP to <a href="https://www.virustotal.com/" rel="noopener">virustotal.com</a> yourself.</li></ol>
</section>
<section class="tarjeta" id="firma">
<h2>Why it isn't signed yet</h2>
<p>A code-signing certificate costs money every year and I'm paying for this project myself. Getting one is my first priority, and the support on Metafy goes toward it. Until then, Windows shows its “protected your PC” warning the first time you run it (<b>More info</b>, then <b>Run anyway</b>). Right-clicking the ZIP, <b>Properties</b>, ticking <b>Unblock</b> before unzipping avoids it.</p>
<p>If you'd rather wait for the signed version, that's completely fair.</p>
</section>
<section class="tarjeta" id="codigo">
<h2>About the code</h2>
<p>For now the code is private. If that changes, I'll say so here.</p>
</section>
<section class="tarjeta" id="dudas">
<h2>Questions</h2>
<p>Write to me: <a href="mailto:manalab.app@gmail.com">manalab.app@gmail.com</a>. I reply myself, usually within a few days.</p>
</section>
<p class="firma">— ManaLab</p>
</div></div>
</div>
</main>
